  <Groups>
    <Group elementId="CPLX-7646" textLabel="3-oxoacyl-[acyl-carrier-protein] reductase, chloroplastic" type="Complex">
      <Xref identifier="CPLX-7646" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="475" width="140" height="100" textColor="666666" fontName="Arial" fontSize="10" borderColor="9900CC" borderStyle="Dashed" borderWidth="2.0" fillColor="F5E6FF" shapeType="Rectangle" zOrder="-1" />
      <Comment>cDNA clones encoding the fatty-acid- biosynthetic enzyme |FRAME: CPLX-7646 3-oxoacyl-[acyl-carrier-protein] reductase, chloroplastic| were isolated from an Arabidopsis thaliana leaf library. The N-terminal end of the coding region shows features typical of a stromal-targeting plastid-transit peptide |CITS: [1575676]|. The deduced amino acid sequences have 41% and 55% identity respectively with the nodG-gene product of Rhizobium meliloti, one of the host-specific genes that restrict infectivity of this bacterium to a small range of host plants.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="CPLX-7646" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="3-oxoacyl-[acyl-carrier-protein] reductase" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="3-ketoacyl-[acyl-carrier-protein] reductase" />
      <Property key="Synonym_3" value="&amp;beta;-ketoacyl-[acyl-carrier-protein] reductase" />
      <Property key="Synonym_4" value="3-oxoacyl-[acp] reductase" />
      <Property key="Synonym_5" value="&amp;beta;-ketoacyl-[acp] reductase" />
      <Property key="ComplexComponents" value="AT1G24360-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="ComponentCount" value="1" />
      <Property key="IsComplex" value="true" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-15237, RXN-15236, RXN-15235, RXN-15234, RXN-15233, RXN-15232, RXN-15231, RXN-4562, RXN-15230" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="9" />
      <Property key="^coefficient" value="4" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="CPLX-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_1575676" />
    </Group>
    <Group elementId="CPLX-7644" textLabel="3-oxoacyl-[acyl-carrier-protein] synthase I, chloroplastic" type="Complex">
      <Xref identifier="CPLX-7644" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="600" centerY="475" width="140" height="100" textColor="666666" fontName="Arial" fontSize="10" borderColor="9900CC" borderStyle="Dashed" borderWidth="2.0" fillColor="F5E6FF" shapeType="Rectangle" zOrder="-1" />
      <Comment source="SRI, caspi">Plant chloroplasts have three isoforms of ketoacyl-[acp] synthase, encoded by |FRAME: AT5G46290 KASI|, |FRAME: G-10790 KASII| and |FRAME: G-8322 KAS III|. KAS III is important for the initial condensation, and accepts only uses (C2)-CoA compounds. KAS I is responsible for further chain elongation up to 14-carbon, and thus is responsible for the synthesis of |FRAME: Palmitoyl-ACPs a palmitoyl-[acp]|. KAS II condenses |FRAME: Palmitoyl-ACPs a palmitoyl-[acp]| with malonyl-ACP to form |FRAME: Stearoyl-ACPs a stearoyl-[acp]|. While KAS I and KAS II use beta-ketoacyl-[acp] as the priming unit, KAS III uses acetyl-CoA. A full length mRNA clone of the |FRAME: AT5G46290 KASI| gene was obtained, and found to share 89.9% identity to the mature castor bean KAS and 82.6 % amino acid identity to the mature barley KAS12 |CITS: [Millar95]|. The transit peptide is 48 amino acid long, followed by a mature polypeptide of 425 amino acids. The gene was deposited at the Plant Gene Register as PGR95-027.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="CPLX-7644" />
      <Property key="ComplexComponents" value="AT5G46290-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="ComponentCount" value="1" />
      <Property key="IsComplex" value="true" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-15239, RXN-15221, RXN-15220, RXN-15219, RXN-15218, RXN-15212, RXN-15211" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="7" />
      <Property key="GOTerms" value="GO:0005759" />
      <Property key="^coefficient" value="2" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="CPLX-*" />
      <Property key="Locations" value="CCI-MIT-LUM-PL" />
    </Group>
  </Groups>
